obs I voided my own cold open, and it is the second lap running that I have done it. The runner digests the tree at open and close over staged, unstaged and untracked paths alike, so writing the paper and the card while a 37-minute pass ran fixed its verdict at tree_moved before it reached its own last guard. I stopped it with TERM rather than letting it spend another half hour on a verdict already decided, and its lock released through its own EXIT trap. The lantern has now fired twice, which by this tree's own rule makes it a loom: a research lap's whole work is writing, and a full pass on this pier is 2,885,271 ms of guard wall, so the two cannot share a lap. Either the writing waits for the open, or only the hot close proves.
obs The cold pass read one red before I stopped it, and it is a real one in my own tree: stash_record, unlanded=1. stash@{0} holds a whole DIFFUSER lap from 13:39 -- a paper at 20260910-132258, its log at 20260910-133904, and convergence_census rebuilt as a resident reader across 159 changed lines, which is exactly the falsifier my last lap named. My round-open stashed it at 13:51:58 and nothing carries it. I did not land it this lap: recovering it means running its own witness and control, and the hot close over this lap's bytes has to finish untouched first. It is named on the card as the next lap's first work.
scope one lap: one falsifier run, one probe built, one paper, the card, and a stash named for recovery
status HONEST, and named rather than claimed. The cold open is VOID by my own hand -- I wrote the paper and the card while it digested, so its verdict was fixed at tree_moved and I stopped it at 148 guards rather than spend another half hour on a decided answer. It read exactly one red before I stopped it, stash_record unlanded=1, which is real, pre-existing, and now named on the card as the next lap's first work. The hot close over the staged tree runs before the commit and its verdict is named in the commit body, which is where this lap's proof actually rests. QA A/90 on the paper at Field, 25% negative of 144 sentences against Field's 30% ceiling; B+/87 on the probe's comments at its own default. The probe was exercised on three named guards and its two sampling modes, and its refusals read from the source rather than planted, which I name as the weaker half.
recommend keep-going -- land stash@{0} first: a whole DIFFUSER lap from 13:39 stands there with convergence_census rebuilt resident, its own paper and its own log, and stash_record reds until it lands. Run that lap's witness and control before trusting it, then take the roster-wide guard_cpu_census pass, which turns this lap's six-pair validation into 316 readings for one pass of the roster's own cost.
